# 12. INTELLIGENCE LAYER

The PRSL-AI Intelligence Layer is AI-agnostic.

PRSL-AI does not depend on one artificial intelligence provider.

The architecture may use:

- Local models
- Apple Foundation Models
- OpenAI models
- Gemini Models
- Claude models
- Specialized models
- Future AI providers
- User-controlled models

AI providers are implementation components.

They are not the architectural identity of PRSL-AI.

The system should be capable of selecting an appropriate intelligence provider according to policy and context.


---

# 13. INTELLIGENCE ROUTER

The Intelligence Router determines which model, service or execution path should handle a request.

Canonical components:

Intent Classifier
    ↓
Context Analyzer
    ↓
Policy & Compliance Checker
    ↓
Model / Service Selector
    ↓
Fallback & Load Balancer
    ↓
Response Formatter


Routing decisions may consider:

- Privacy
- Capability Match
- Context Match
- Latency
- Cost
- Availability
- Policy
- User preferences
- Device capabilities


---

# 14. iRIEL INTELLIGENCE SERVER

The iRiel Intelligence Server provides infrastructure for Personal Intelligence and durable execution.

Responsibilities may include:

- Intelligence Routing
- Context Services
- Memory Services
- Workflow Services
- Integration Services
- Policy Services
- Intelligence Workers
- Durable Workflow Workers
- Server-side orchestration

The Intelligence Server is infrastructure.

It is not the owner of the user's identity.

It does not redefine @iriel.


---

# 15. TEMPORAL — DURABLE WORKFLOW ENGINE

Temporal is used as a durable workflow execution engine within the iRiel Intelligence Server architecture.

Temporal may manage:

- Workflow IDs
- Workflow state
- Activities
- Timers
- Signals
- Retries
- Failures
- Execution history
- Recovery state

Temporal does not replace:

- @iriel
- Context
- Memory
- Identity
- Privacy
- Security
- Personal Intelligence

Temporal provides durable execution.

It does not provide human identity.


---

# 16. WORKFLOW CONTINUITY

Workflows belong to the Personal Intelligence Environment rather than to a specific device.

Therefore:

iPhone
    ↓
Workflow
    ↓
Personal Intelligence Environment
    ↓
Temporal
    ↓
Desktop
    ↓
Workflow Continuation


A workflow should be capable of surviving:

- Device changes
- Network interruptions
- Device shutdown
- Worker failures
- Session interruptions
- Temporary service failures

The user should not need to recreate a workflow simply because the execution environment changed.


